# 3. `US?/O_o`: the temporal gauge rail

The temporal rail contains:

```text
LL
MM
NN
```

with:

```text
LL
 previous phase

MM
 present phase

NN
 next phase
```

Its linear form is:

```text
o-LL-MM-NN-o
```

Interpretation:

```text
opening o
 previous boundary

LL
 phase entering the transition

MM
 phase under present gauge

NN
 phase produced by the transition

closing o
 forward boundary
```

The temporal recurrence is:

```text
NN = Δ(MM, gauge)
```

After one shift:

```text
LL' = MM
MM' = NN
NN' = Δ(NN, next gauge)
```

Therefore:

```text
o-LL-MM-NN-o
```

is a three-phase moving window rather than three fixed memory regions.

