# 4. Expanded `US?/O_o` notation

The full temporal-gauge notation is:

```text
Δ-(US . ?)-(/ . O)-(_ . o)-Δ
```

This contains three paired character cells enclosed by delta boundaries:

```text
opening Δ
 directed entry

(US . ?)
 unresolved scope paired with query

(/ . O)
 branch or division paired with oriented object

(_ . o)
 retained place paired with local object

closing Δ
 directed exit
```

The three paired cells correspond to the temporal window:

```text
LL = (US . ?)

MM = (/ . O)

NN = (_ . o)
```

Therefore:

```text
o-LL-MM-NN-o
```

expands to:

```text
Δ-(US . ?)-(/ . O)-(_ . o)-Δ
```

The correspondence is:

```text
LL
=
(US . ?)

MM
=
(/ . O)

NN
=
(_ . o)
```

Operational interpretation:

```text
LL = (US . ?)
 the previous phase carries an unresolved state and a query

MM = (/ . O)
 the present phase applies a branch/division gauge to an oriented object

NN = (_ . o)
 the next phase retains the resolved place and emits a local object
```

