# 9. Gauge-injected notation

Your second expanded expression is:

```text
(
 omi---imo
 XOR
 (o|O)-US?/O_o-(o|O)
)
XOR
(
 omi---imo
 XOR
 (o|O)-US?/O_o-(o|O)
)
```

Define the gauge-wrapped traversal as:

```text
G =
(o|O)-US?/O_o-(o|O)
```

Then the expression becomes:

```text
(omi---imo XOR G)
XOR
(omi---imo XOR G)
```

By associativity and commutativity of XOR:

```text
=
omi---imo
XOR G
XOR omi---imo
XOR G
```

Reorder identical terms:

```text
=
(omi---imo XOR omi---imo)
XOR
(G XOR G)
```

Each pair cancels:

```text
=
NULL XOR NULL
```

Therefore:

```text
=
NULL
```

In paired notation:

```text
=
(NULL . NULL)
```

So the full identity is:

```text
(
 omi---imo XOR (o|O)-US?/O_o-(o|O)
)
XOR
(
 omi---imo XOR (o|O)-US?/O_o-(o|O)
)
=
(NULL . NULL)
```

This is the self-cancellation law for a gauge-injected scope state.

