# 10. Meaning of `(o|O)`

The notation:

```text
(o|O)
```

is an orientation choice.

It contains:

```text
o
 local or low orientation

O
 projected or high orientation

|
 branch selection between them
```

Therefore:

```text
(o|O)-US?/O_o-(o|O)
```

means:

```text
select an orientation
apply the US?/O_o traversal
resolve into an orientation
```

Expanded directional possibilities include:

```text
o-US?/O_o-o
o-US?/O_o-O
O-US?/O_o-o
O-US?/O_o-O
```

These represent:

```text
o → o
 local persistence

o → O
 local-to-projected traversal

O → o
 projected-to-local traversal

O → O
 projected persistence
```

The vertical bar does not mean that both states are simultaneously selected.

It exposes the orientation branch that the gauge must resolve.

