# 12. Transition example in notation

Start with:

```text
LL = (US . ?)
```

This means:

```text
unresolved previous state
with an active query
```

The gauge moves the state into:

```text
MM = (/ . O)
```

and the Blackboard moves:

```text
US → GS
```

So the present paired state is:

```text
(GS . (/ . O))
```

Interpretation:

```text
the source relation has become known,
the output remains unresolved,
and the present operator is projecting through / toward O
```

The next state becomes:

```text
NN = (_ . o)
```

and the Blackboard resolves:

```text
GS → FS
```

The next paired state is:

```text
(FS . (_ . o))
```

Complete transition:

```text
(US . (US . ?))
→
(GS . (/ . O))
→
(FS . (_ . o))
```

Using the rail notation:

```text
omi-(RS . US)-imo
 .
Δ-(US . ?)-Δ
```

advances through:

```text
omi-(FS . GS)-imo
 .
Δ-(/ . O)-Δ
```

and closes as:

```text
omi-(FS . FS)-imo
 .
Δ-(_ . o)-Δ
```

The compact conceptual path is:

```text
query
→ gauge
→ place
```

and:

```text
US
→ GS
→ FS
```

