# 13. Reverse transition

The reverse or abductive path begins from an observed result:

```text
RS
=
Unknown Known
```

The temporal object begins at:

```text
(_ . o)
```

The reverse gauge asks for its source:

```text
(/ . O)
```

and returns to query:

```text
(US . ?)
```

So the reverse path is:

```text
(FS . (_ . o))
→
(RS . (/ . O))
→
(US . (US . ?))
```

The epistemic path is:

```text
FS → RS → US
```

while constructive resolution is:

```text
US → GS → FS
```

Thus the two traversals are:

```text
forward:
US → GS → FS

reverse:
FS → RS → US
```

These are the two sides of the circular slide ruler.

