# 14. Proper notation grammar

The grammar can be written as:

```text
<Protocol>
 ::= "(" <ScopeRail> "." <TemporalRail> ")"

<ScopeRail>
 ::= "omi-" <ForwardScope> "-" <ReverseScope> "-imo"

<ForwardScope>
 ::= "(" "FS" "." "GS" ")"

<ReverseScope>
 ::= "(" "RS" "." "US" ")"

<TemporalRail>
 ::= "Δ-" <Previous> "-" <Present> "-" <Next> "-Δ"

<Previous>
 ::= "(" "US" "." "?" ")"

<Present>
 ::= "(" "/" "." "O" ")"

<Next>
 ::= "(" "_" "." "o" ")"

<Orientation>
 ::= "o" | "O"

<OrientationGate>
 ::= "(" "o" "|" "O" ")"
```

The canonical expanded object is:

```text
(
 omi-(FS . GS)-(RS . US)-imo
 .
 Δ-(US . ?)-(/ . O)-(_ . o)-Δ
)
```

The canonical compact object is:

```text
(omi---imo . US?/O_o)
```

