# 15. Rewrite identities

## Identity pairing

```text
A XOR NULL = A
```

Therefore:

```text
(omi---imo . US?/O_o)
XOR
(NULL . NULL)
=
(omi---imo . US?/O_o)
```

## Self-cancellation

```text
A XOR A = NULL
```

Therefore:

```text
(omi---imo . US?/O_o)
XOR
(omi---imo . US?/O_o)
=
(NULL . NULL)
```

## Reversible gauge injection

Let:

```text
S = omi---imo
G = (o|O)-US?/O_o-(o|O)
```

Then:

```text
S' = S XOR G
```

Applying the same gauge again:

```text
S' XOR G
=
(S XOR G) XOR G
=
S XOR (G XOR G)
=
S XOR NULL
=
S
```

So:

```text
gauge injection
followed by
the same gauge injection
```

restores the original scope rail.

## Difference comparison

For two states:

```text
P₁ = (S₁ . T₁)
P₂ = (S₂ . T₂)
```

their difference is:

```text
P₁ XOR P₂
=
(S₁ XOR S₂ . T₁ XOR T₂)
```

This reports separately:

```text
scope difference
temporal-gauge difference
```

